# Hollowtrunk Grove - the fifth island of the library's plan The Last Green World (SL11, Verdance)
# A grove of five giant trees (Raft's giant firs and birches from Balboa) on a low green island, a wooden hut or a deck
# on posts at the foot of each. The Seedkeepers' greenhouse (an open shelter) stands by the south beach with its water
# tower and an old token machine; a zipline runs from the deck at the second trunk to the fourth; the seed store sits at
# the foot of the biggest trunk, and between its roots a hollow runs down: the root hole. Bees hum in the birches. Burr
# the goat stands by a vine-choked cache in the north-east. Quest "The Hollow Trees" (12 steps): the greenhouse, the
# watering rota, the water tank plans in the water tower, the zipline to the fourth trunk, the water pipe plans in its
# store, the purifier plans in the crown box, the large storage plans in the seed store, the seed drawers, Ranger log 6,
# the root hole (it brings Rootweave Caves).
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe hollowtrunk_grove) through the editor's own operations. Points (metres over the
# sea): the greenhouse pad 1.6 m round 0 -40, the water tower x -16..-11.5, z -46..-41.5; the trunks T1 (fir) 0 10,
# T2 (fir) -32 -6, T3 (birch) 30 -14, T4 (fir) -26 36, T5 (birch) 28 30, their pads at 2 m; T2's deck x -27..-22.5,
# z -10..-5.5, T4's deck x -22..-17.5, z 30..34.5; the seed store x 6..10.5, z 14..17; the root hole 0.6 m at -6 2.
include lib_sea
include lib_features
include lib_huts
include lib_gravity
include lib_verdance
include lib_ni8
